WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Welcome to the CETECH Delivery Engine staff walkthrough for release candidate 1.0.0-rc.2. In this short overview you will learn where everyday delivery work happens, and what customers and staff each see.

2
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:40.000
In WordPress admin, open Delivery Engine. This is the home for delivery configuration for your store.

3
00:00:40.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Your everyday starting point is Delivery Settings. Most day-to-day work happens here — not in Legacy Delivery Rules.

4
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Think of three layers. Default Settings apply store-wide. Product-Specific Settings can change one product. Variation-Specific Settings can change one variation. Prefer inheritance unless something truly needs to differ.

5
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Delivery Settings Preview is read-only. It shows what will actually apply for a product or variation, including Ready or Needs configuration.

6
00:01:40.000 --> 00:02:00.000
At a high level: Delivery Offers are the choices customers see. Destination Zones describe where a choice applies. Rate Cards connect an offer and zone to a delivery charge. You configure products in Delivery Settings; these pages support that setup.

7
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:20.000
After a customer pays, staff open the order and find Delivery information — fulfilment, delivery method, delivery option, estimated delivery, and charge. You do not need technical metadata for normal work.

8
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:40.000
Remember: Delivery Settings for everyday work, Preview to confirm, and Delivery information on orders after purchase. Next videos go deeper into each step.
